<title>LEBANON: Solidere signs $29 mln power station deal.</title>
<headline>Solidere signs $29 mln power station deal.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's biggest company Solidere signed a $29 million contract with a consortium of Japanese, Lebanese and U.S. companies to build an electric power station in central Beirut, a source in Solidere said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The contract was signed last Wednesday with the Lebanese company Matelec, General Electric of the United States and Hitachi of Japan to build a power station in the war-ravaged city centre which Solidere is rebuilding, he told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;Work on the project will start at the beginning of 1997 and is expected to finish in two years,&quot; the source, who asked not to be identified, added.</p>
</text>
